  "learn": {
    "title": "Dual Sensor Watch",
    "body": "Power DHT22 at 3V3/GND with DATA on GPIO23. Wire pot end1 to 3V3, end2 to GND and wiper to GPIO34. Wire GPIO18 → 220 Ω → LED → GND. GPIO34 is ADC1, so it can be read while WiFi is active; never feed it 5 V.\n\nJoin VoltNet and map the 12-bit ADC reading 0–4095 to a 20–40°C limit. Sample every 100 ms. Turn the alarm on only when temperature is at least the limit AND humidity is at least 70%. Turn it off when temperature falls to limit minus 2°C OR humidity falls to 65%. Otherwise retain state. Serve /status as t=32.0;limit=30;h=75.0;alarm=ON, using current readings and one decimal for the sensor values.\n\nAt knob 50%, set 32°C / 60%: off. Raise humidity to 75%: on. Set 29°C / 68%: retain on. Lower humidity to 60%: off. Request /status in the hot/humid phase. A warm dry room must not trigger this two-condition alarm.",
    "links": []
  },
